{"kind":"entry","id":"derived:claude-code:user_correction:c6a27d9a-b193-4afa-8e98-5334e7fafd33:bf4226c1-63d3-4a59-89ba-4acd70d1800b","type_name":"user_correction","type_version":1,"type_hash":"8f1dfdc7a2dfd699da33dcc074d6a996fa89c7a584c84044dd4c4852dbd539ad","recorded_at":"2026-09-28T17:56:31.543Z","source":"derived:claude-code","run_id":null,"workflow":null,"actor":null,"cwd":".","repo":null,"git_sha":null,"branch":"HEAD","properties":{"occurred_at":"2026-09-11T23:30:28.931Z","project":"-Users-spikedpunchvictim-projects-aide","session_id":"c6a27d9a-b193-4afa-8e98-5334e7fafd33","tool_name":"ExitPlanMode"},"na":[],"evidence_text":"We are in planning mode where no code will be written until we have worked through the important details of this product. Lets name the product ascend. The CLI, written using oclif, can be 'asc'. For type definitions, we should use zod for enforcement. When a new entry type is defined, the LLM should be able to use the CLI to define the name and type. When a new entry is added for a type, it is validated using zod. Invalid shapes will report an error, and tell the LLM how to correct it. Some fields should also be marked as required, default optional. For each defined type, we will also want to define when an LLM should record it. Recording an item should be cheap for the LLM - but its cost will not be zero. What are your thoughts? What are we missing?","ascend_version":"0.0.0","schema_version":6}
