{"kind":"entry","id":"derived:claude-code:user_correction:f98c0c91-35b7-428d-8fc2-4f2da839633d:d69c8e3f-ef15-4580-8d90-57081549e3d5","type_name":"user_correction","type_version":1,"type_hash":"8f1dfdc7a2dfd699da33dcc074d6a996fa89c7a584c84044dd4c4852dbd539ad","recorded_at":"2026-09-28T17:56:31.543Z","source":"derived:claude-code","run_id":null,"workflow":null,"actor":null,"cwd":".","repo":null,"git_sha":null,"branch":"integrations","properties":{"occurred_at":"2026-09-01T23:18:53.305Z","project":"-Users-spikedpunchvictim-projects-grizzly-grizzly-wip","session_id":"f98c0c91-35b7-428d-8fc2-4f2da839633d","tool_name":"ExitPlanMode"},"na":[],"evidence_text":"Feedback:\r\r* Vendor Guide: Should this be a .json file the server reads in, and the CLI can reference it as well, instead of having to parse code for the data?\r* Vendor Registry: Should this also be a json file that can be referenced by the CLI?\r* scripts/test-integration.js -> scripts/test-integration.mjs (adding the mjs extension to match the other script in the repo)\r* For the \"pick a vendor\" is not \"pick a provider\": Can we pick Loki, and have it setup the integration for Loki (Otel, etc), just like we do in the dashboard\r* For Multi-identity seeding does not exist: Is your recommendation that we build this into our solution or something we want to build into our harness in general?\r* Activities - props is accepted by the schema and never read: We are storing the props though, correct? If not, this is a bug we should add to our task list\r* Integration idempotency has no server support: This is something we should address. Unless you have a good readon not to, we should at least allow the user to update certain fields for their integration. Deleting and recreating is a poor developer/user experience. We should also add a \"find by name\" for the integrations. The Dashboard will mostl likely need this.\r* Verification coverage is uneven and must be published, not implied: This is a good point. If we do select a non-vendor integration, we should have a list of vnedors or a default vendor to use in those scenarios. Otherwise, what are we writing to? and whatever vendor we do choose, we will know how to query it\r* Stale BullMQ schedulers: If we do wire that in - I don't see why we would - then we would need to delete those before running. Lets see if we can get away from having to wire that in.\r* For stack ownership, we will need write a state file, or something similar. This way we can show who owns it. If we do build a service to bring up and down a local stack, this is something that could be wired into the MCP server, which can track the running instances, when they were started, who/what owns them, etc.\r* For .devconfig/fastify-server.env: We should have, alongside the config files, our own fastify server env file. This way we can control what the env variables are when running these demos/verifications.\r* ADR number: 020: We do not need to worry about what ADRs exist in other branches. We create them in the feature branch, and reconcile them at merge time - even if it does mean we need to update all of our references throughout the documentation. We may move to a timestamp model in the future to avoid this scenario.\r* There should be 1 config file per test scenario\r* \r\r\r\rOutside of this task:\r\r* We need explicit tasks that capture implementing sigv4 and jwt-bearer-assertion. We should find other vendors, that we can run locally, that support these features so we can test locally.","ascend_version":"0.0.0","schema_version":6}
